# Physics and restitution
@scenario tutorial_lesson_44
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/44_physics_lab.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt open_physics]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: The two circles start with equal velocity and travel toward an identical wall. Compare how far they travel after the collision.
@label lab
> Run the collision -> demo
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label demo
# region open_physics
[jes push scripts/scenes/physics_lab.jes label compare]
# endregion
@label compare
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/physics_lab.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt restitution]
ginger: Change the smaller restitution value to 1. Reopen and compare. The world resolves the collision each frame, so the animation comes from the simulation.
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_44]
[flag tutorial_done_44]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_9]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Which comparison isolates restitution?
> Change both circles’ speed and mass. -> practice_hint
> Keep both velocities fixed and change just restitution. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: The rebound coefficient changes the response to collision.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: The rebound coefficient changes the response to collision.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: What does restitution control?
> The rebound after a collision. -> correct
> How many tiles are in the map. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
ginger: The rebound coefficient changes the response to collision.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The rebound coefficient changes the response to collision.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
